From 7e038af63e3ab2f7c698e250b37606f76dbda2fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Sandrock <luca.sandrock@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:21:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pipewire): meter peaks for nodes with unpositioned
 channels

The peak monitor refused to meter any node whose per-channel volumes
could not be mapped onto the capture stream's named channels. Native
PipeWire clients such as Spotify negotiate their stream format with
unpositioned channel positions (SPA_AUDIO_FLAG_UNPOSITIONED, reported as
UNK/UNK), so the node's channel list is [Unknown, Unknown] while the
autoconnected capture stream is positioned [FrontLeft, FrontRight]. No
channel matched, the volume vector stayed shorter than the channel count,
and handleProcess() logged "is missing channels present in capture
stream" and returned early every buffer, leaving the per-app meter flat.

The peak computation itself is position-agnostic: it reads samples by
channel index. Only the optional inverse volume scaling needs a matched
per-channel volume, and that step is already guarded by an emptiness
check. When the volumes cannot be fully mapped (unpositioned channels,
partial matches, or unusual layouts), drop the volume vector and meter by
index instead of refusing the node. Nodes with known channels still match
fully, keep their volumes, and behave exactly as before.
---
 src/services/pipewire/peak.cpp | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/services/pipewire/peak.cpp b/src/services/pipewire/peak.cpp
index 2aec7f5..4cae48b 100644
--- a/src/services/pipewire/peak.cpp
+++ b/src/services/pipewire/peak.cpp
@@ -292,11 +292,9 @@ void PwPeakStream::handleProcess() {
 				}
 			}
 
+			// native clients (spotify) negotiate unpositioned UNK channels that don't map to the capture stream's named channels; meter by index and skip inverse volume scaling instead of refusing the node
 			if (volumes.length() != channelCount) {
-				qCCritical(logPeak) << this->node
-				                    << "is missing channels present in capture stream. Node channels:"
-				                    << nchannels << "Stream channels:" << this->monitor->mChannels;
-				return;
+				volumes.clear();
 			}
 		}
 	}
